  "problem": "If $X={a,c,a,b,a,b,d}$, then $|X|=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The cardinality of a finite set $X$ is the number of elements in $X.$ \n\nLet's start by listing all the elements of $X:$\n\n$$\na,\\,b,\\,c,\\,d\n$$\n\nNote that only *unique* elements are counted. In other words, duplicate elements are *not* counted separately.\n\nSince $X$ has $4$ elements, its cardinality is $|X|=\\text{4}.$",
